 "confidence":"0.9992 (high alert threshold 0.24)",
 "explanation":"The highest statistical measure (max) indicates the largest packet size, which is indicative of a large payload. The lowest statistical measure (min) shows the smallest inter-arrival time, suggesting a short delay between connections. The standard deviation of packet sizes (stddev) provides insight into variability within the flow, indicating potential issues with packet fragmentation or congestion. Together, these statistics suggest a potentially malicious activity, raising suspicion.", "mitigation":"Monitor for unusual patterns such as rapid growth in packet size or frequent retransmissions."}
